{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790336694,"nonce":"zhGHGxax3SeEByVkKKPvmvP+KJ8=","message":"What an embedder needs from this (caribou, where Python modules use other languages' modules through zyntax_embed::foreign, 98d28403):\n\n1. A foreign object is awaitable. Caribou's futures reach Python as foreign objects (a gpu plugin's device.queueWorkDone(queue), device.mapBuffer(...)); the embedder can answer ready() and await() on them through Foreign::invoke, and can settle them from other threads. 'await f' on a foreign value should suspend the coroutine until the embedder says it is done, rather than block the thread, since the embedder's scheduler runs other work meanwhile.\n2. An exported async def is callable by the embedder: caribou would publish it as returning a core future and drive it to completion from one of its tasks. It needs to know a function is async (TypedFunction.is_async survives to the typed AST/HIR it reads) and a way to poll or drive the returned coroutine and read its value or exception.\n\nThe test in crates/zyntax_python/tests/foreign.rs has a stand-in embedder that could grow an awaitable.","files":null}]}